m. Fresh pushed-head CI and substantive re-review remain required at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/66/checks."
  "2026-11-08T18:09:15.028Z",codex-agent,"Continuation round 5: inspected clean existing branch and remote head 513cfc7, existing PR #66 and this item; origin/main is already an ancestor. Preserve prior work. Verified three remaining findings. General rules: every schema input must be byte-bound even when it aliases settings; semantic schema identity must ignore object-key order but preserve arrays; all diagnostics must use the same captured status registry. Audit every caller/digest and cover SDK, CLI JSON/TOON, non-git and packed npm/Bun consumers. No transcript reads or duplicate work items."
  "2026-11-08T18:15:11.451Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: all lintCorpus call sites checked: engine lintItems and incremental evaluation already supply configured registries; repairs now resolves roles directly from the guarded private schema. All semantic digest callers use canonical sourceDigest except repair schema context; that caller now reuses it. Retained-file fingerprints intentionally omit ordinary settings so independent extension sections remain compatible; schema references to settings instead compare the full pre-hook raw document at the private handoff, for every section and normalized alias. Also normalize whitespace in excluded-state guards using the SDK path rule. New regression corpus covers all four sections, three aliases, both hook timings; 32 seeded recursive key permutations plus ordered arrays; 15 renamed lifecycle cases via SDK and real no-git JSON/TOON CLI. Packed npm/Bun acceptance covers all three classes. No existing regression was removed or weakened. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication and 120/120 docstrings passed."
  "2026-11-08T18:18:56.694Z",codex-agent,"Focused build/typecheck and repairs/settings/model tests passed 31/31. Audit correction: whitespace in excluded-state paths is already refused by the pinned SDK guarded loader; its extra regression passed even with the proposed early-guard trim reverted. Dropped that redundant code edit and retained both original and whitespace refusal cases. Settings-as-schema alias normalization remains necessary and revert-sensitive. No SDK gap or additional defect is claimed."
  "2026-11-08T18:20:38.346Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs ran only in disposable package copies: removing the settingsIsSchema raw-byte comparison makes repair schema aliases fail (exit 1); replacing sourceDigest(schema) with raw schema makes repair schema identity fail (exit 1); removing the captured resolveRuntimeStatusRegistry argument makes repair questions preserve fail (exit 1). Each changes only the relevant production expression. Restored implementation passes 3/3 regressions (66.5 seconds); the original worktree was never mutated for proofs. Focused build/settings/repairs/model suite passes 31/31; linked new class tests also completed. Full serial npm/Bun release gates are next, with isolated HOME/global Git configuration and at most two test workers."
  "2026-11-08T18:21:03.464Z",codex-agent,Linked class regression execution passed 3/3 in 73.4 seconds. Optional strict health currently reports one pre-existing managed pm-github host/extension version-skew warning (pinned host 2026.11.4 versus managed extension host 2026.11.7); tracked by pm-lint-managed-extension-health-skew. No pin bumps or managed extension mutations in this review fix. This is separate from the required release gates; final evidence will report the warning explicitly.
  "2026-11-08T18:35:09.341Z",codex-agent,"Packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx focused acceptance passed 1/1 (179.8 seconds). First full npm release run passed 205/205 source tests, 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 32 sources, identity/privacy, typecheck, lint, zero duplication and docstrings, then the registry advisory endpoint returned a transient request error at audit:prod (623.0 seconds total). Immediate identical audit:prod retry passed with zero vulnerabilities. Rerunning the complete npm release gate, then Bun serially; no test or threshold changes. Positive unchanged settings/schema alias assertions also passed inside that full source suite."
  "2026-11-08T18:47:59.192Z",codex-agent,"Extended class audit found the same semantic-ordering defect in inline schema: contextRevision also consumed the raw settings string. The final implementation hashes parsed captured settings and effective schema together through canonical sourceDigest; raw settings bytes remain independently fenced for safety. Property regressions now permute nested keys in both inline and file schemas (32 each), retain array-order sensitivity, and packed npm/Bun acceptance covers both sources. Stopped the older gate after its 205/205 source tests and 100/100/100/100 coverage passed, before final acceptance completed, to rerun all final gates against this expanded fix. Earlier green results are intermediate evidence, not final-head certification."
  "2026-11-08T18:50:01.231Z",codex-agent,"Final class implementation and focused tests passed 3/3 (70.1 seconds). Final disposable behavioral proofs: removing settings-as-schema byte binding, replacing canonical context hashing with raw JSON order, passing raw settings instead of the captured parsed document (inline schema), and removing the configured status-registry argument each independently exit 1. Restored final implementation passes 3/3. The inline-only revert passes the file-schema permutations before failing on inline schema, proving both storage paths separately. Typecheck, lint and zero duplication passed; final serial npm/Bun gates now follow expanded packed acceptance."
  "2026-11-08T19:22:33.012Z",codex-agent,"Final validation: npm run release:check passed in 699.6 seconds; bun run release:check passed in 994.0 seconds. Each passed 205/205 tests across 11 suites, all 32 authored sources at 100/100/100/100, 120/120 docstrings, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, zero-vulnerability production audit, package contents, changelog and release attestation, plus 1/1 packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance. Final focused class tests passed 3/3 (70.1 seconds); final linked pm test execution passed 3/3 (81.8 seconds); expanded standalone packed acceptance passed 1/1 (215.3 seconds). All tests ran with at most two workers, serial full gates and isolated HOME/global Git configuration. Four disposable expression reverts each failed; restored final implementation passed 3/3. Earlier advisory-endpoint error was transient, its identical retry and both final gates passed. Fresh fetch confirms origin/main remains included and remote PR branch unchanged. Optional strict health still has the previously recorded managed extension version-skew warning, tracked separately by pm-lint-managed-extension-health-skew. Implementation is ready for orchestrator verification on existing PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/66; do not close this item. Review threads remain untouched and pushed-head CI/bot verification is external evidence."
  "2026-11-08T19:22:56.675Z",codex-agent,"Validation environment clarification: isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration apply to both full release gates and their packed consumers. Focused class and revert tests use real disposable non-git trackers, with actual CLI calls additionally fencing Git discovery and executables. The at-most-two-worker limit applies to every test invocation. No code changed after the final gates."
  "2026-11-08T19:55:41.832Z",codex-agent,"Continuation round 6: package worktree is clean and matches the existing PR remote head; origin/main is already included. Both unresolved CodeRabbit findings are valid: read failures must classify hook-induced invalidation without masking pre-existing SDK errors, and schema/settings aliases must bind file identity rather than path spelling. Auditing all repair entry points, shared readers, JSON/TOON receipts, packed npm/Bun consumers and non-git trackers. Retain prior fixes and append-only tracker evidence; no duplicate PR or item."
  "2026-11-08T20:01:20.709Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: repair planning is the only reader that binds captured settings across hooks; ordinary lint and incremental adapters use the shared SDK section reader without a captured repair receipt. SDK and lint repair command share previewAuthoringRepairs, so JSON/TOON stale receipts retain writes=0 and exit_code=2. Witness paths use realpath containment; sidecar publication already uses device/inode ownership checks. Fixed repair aliases by checking normalized paths and device/inode identities before hooks. Error classification reuses resolveConfig for captured lint validity and preserves pre-existing malformed/invalid SDK errors plus native I/O errors. New non-git adversarial matrix covers document shapes, every rule control, changed/unchanged invalid settings and real same-inode case-varied aliases; packed npm/Node and native Bun consumers repeat both classes. No additional package instance or SDK gap found; latest review has no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-11-08T20:04:04.085Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in disposable copies: removing only the new SDK read-error classification makes node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"repair read errors\" test/repairs.test.ts fail 0/1, exit 1, on the leaked settings_section_document_malformed error. Replacing only schemaUsesSettings with the old normalized path-string comparison makes node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"repair schema aliases compare\" test/repairs.test.ts fail 0/1, exit 1, on SETTINGS.JSON (same device/inode, different spelling). Restoring both implementations passes the combined class suite 3/3, exit 0. The unchanged package worktree also passes 3/3, and pm test --run --progress --only-last passes the linked command without recording run artifacts (tracking_disabled). Typecheck, lint, documented declarations and zero-duplication checks pass. No existing test was weakened or deleted. Proceeding with serial full npm/Bun gates using isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration, at most two workers."
  "2026-11-08T20:17:24.011Z",codex-agent,Portability self-review found that same-inode alias fixtures must reuse an already existing case-insensitive spelling instead of unconditionally creating a hard link; packed cleanup must unlink only aliases the fixture actually created. Corrected both fixture paths without dropping assertions. Intentionally stopped the first npm gate before completion to make this correction; no full-gate pass is claimed for that partial run. Repeating both behavioral reverts and the restored focused suite before fresh serial full npm/Bun gates.
  "2026-11-08T20:20:33.358Z",codex-agent,"Final portable fixtures verified: both production-only behavioral reverts still fail independently (0/1 each, exit 1), and restoration passes the class suite 3/3 in 129.4 seconds. The linked pm test rerun also passes 3/3 using the final files and records no source-tracker run artifacts. Build, typecheck, lint, 0 percent duplication and all 121 documented declarations pass. Starting fresh full npm and Bun release gates serially from this final source/test state; the deliberately stopped earlier gate remains incomplete evidence."
  "2026-11-08T20:33:29.010Z",codex-agent,"Final same-class audit reproduced an additional path-normalization defect: a direct whitespace-padded excluded schema path (for example, \" runtime/fields.json \") produced a successful preview because the exclusion guard compared untrimmed text while the SDK trims it. The existing corpus covered whitespace before schema/.., which accidentally normalized away the prefix. Fixed the guard to trim before resolving, matching alias detection and the SDK loader. Expanded the existing regression across all four schema sections, all six excluded directories and five path spellings; packed npm/Bun consumers also cover every section/directory with direct padded references. This is in-scope closure of the normalization class on the existing item. Stopped the second partial gate for this reproduced correction; neither partial run is a full-gate pass."
  "2026-11-08T20:39:37.302Z",codex-agent,"Final class closure proofs: three independent production-only behavioral reverts fail 0/1 each, exit 1: remove SDK read-error classification (leaked typed document error), replace file identity with path-string equality (SETTINGS.JSON alias missed), or remove trimming from the excluded-state guard (unsafe reference silently accepted). Restoring the final implementation passes 4/4 class tests in 281.4 seconds. The linked expanded pm test also passes 4/4 with no source-tracker run artifacts. The additional normalized-path corpus covers 4 schema sections x 6 excluded directories x 5 spellings and preserves every previous assertion; packed npm/Bun consumers cover all section/directory pairs too. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication and 121/121 docstrings pass. No further unnormalized schema-path check was found in the package. Both earlier full-gate attempts were deliberately interrupted for corrections and are not passing evidence. Running final serial npm/Bun gates now from this complete class implementation, with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration and at most two workers."
  "2026-11-08T21:10:07.673Z",codex-agent,"Applied the original task local-time condition to full release gates: the final npm attempt ran 1742.2 seconds under heavy shared-host load and was still in the repair model. Stopped deliberately because combined npm/Bun full certification is not expected within the requested local hour. Partial root summary: 161 passed, 0 failed, 3 canceled by the stop; this is incomplete evidence, not a full-gate pass or coverage certification. Full Bun release:check is deferred too. Completing isolated-HOME changed-file settings/repairs tests, standalone packed npm/Node and native Bun acceptance, remaining static release checks and final tracker health; unchanged full npm/Bun/100-percent gates must certify the pushed head in CI. Both earlier partial attempts were also stopped for corrections, never counted as passes."
  "2026-11-08T21:24:23.052Z",codex-agent,"Round 6 final implementation: PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc61Dsue now returns stale_revision for hook-invalidated previously valid settings while preserving pre-existing typed SDK and native I/O errors. PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc61Dsui now detects settings/schema aliases by device/inode before hooks; class audit additionally fixed untrimmed excluded-state paths across every schema section. Final node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/settings.test.ts test/repairs.test.ts passes 32/32 with no failures/skips (427.8 seconds). npm run test:install passes 1/1 packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx consumers from the final artifact (469.8 seconds), including invalidation, alias identity and every excluded section/directory pair. Class/linked pm suites pass 4/4; three separate function/expression reverts each fail 0/1, with restoration green. Typecheck, lint, build, 121/121 docstrings, zero duplication, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry-run (105 files) and release-publish attestation pass at unchanged thresholds. Source tracker run artifacts remain disabled. Full npm/Bun release and 100-percent coverage certification remain pending CI under the recorded local time bound; no complete local full-gate pass is claimed. Clean isolated-profile tracker health previously passed 10/10; normal-profile managed-extension skew is already tracked separately. Rechecking final tracker health, changelog and identity after this last write before commit/push. No PM CLI/SDK defect found; immutable linked-command replacement used the supported remove/add operation without losing any test coverage. Releasing only this implementation claim; retain in_progress for orchestrator verification, and leave review threads untouched."
  "2026-11-09T01:46:37.359Z",pi-glm,"Final round (head 26a1917): fixed both CodeRabbit Minor findings in src/repairs.ts with the smallest change.\n1) PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc61Ep3D (plan identity): plan_key hashed the whole SDK schema-loading context, so loader warnings (e.g. schema/fields.json changing from {} to malformed {) changed plan_key for the same effective schema. contextRevision now hashes only the effective schema plus the file-backed type definitions; warnings and staging metadata are diagnostics, not identity.\n2) PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc61Ep3G (case aliases): the excluded-directory guard compared the first path segment exactly, so RUNTIME/fields.json could reference the excluded runtime directory on case-insensitive volumes. Guard now compares excluded names and the first path segment case-insensitively after Unicode NFC normalization."
  "2026-11-09T01:46:41.426Z",pi-glm,"Revert proofs (local mutation, this worktree):\n- Plan-identity fix reverted (contextRevision hashing the whole schema-loading context again): 'repair plan identity excludes schema loader warnings' FAILS; restored: PASSES.\n- Case-alias guard reverted (exact-name Object.hasOwn comparison): 'repair schema path guards reject case aliases of excluded directories' FAILS; restored: PASSES.\nGates at head: settings+repairs suites 34/34 pass; typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication (0% clone pairs), changelog:check and identity:check all clean. dist/ is not committed by this repo. No thread replies, no merge, no release."
  "2026-11-09T01:53:16.135Z",pi-glm,"pm test --run note: the full-suite linked command (npm run build + settings/repairs suites) was terminated by the runner's fixed 120s timeout at 119.5s with 31 passed/0 failed so far (host load artifact, not a test failure); the identical command run directly completes in ~126s with 34/34 pass. The three focused linked commands all passed, including the new regression pair."
